window.docContents[216].resolve({"/Types-and-expressions/#Core-C______--Types-and-expressions":{"contents":"The typing and evaluation rules of the basic constructions of Expr. The typing rules are constructors of Semantics.HasType and Semantics.LHasType, which Typing.expr and Typing.lval implement. The evaluation rules are constructors of Semantics.Eval, which Eval.expr implements, each rule in the comment of the case that implements it. An lvalue yields the location of the object it designates, , and every other expression its value, . A premise  converts a result where a value is required, . The trace of bin/corecpp trace cites the rules by these names. Calls, lambdas, this, members and the uses of the library have their rules in the later chapters.\n\nWhere C++17 leaves the evaluation order unspecified, Core C++ evaluates left to right. The last section holds the composite and recursive types, objects and pointers, whose expressions are lvalues.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Core C++","header":"3. Types and expressions","id":"/Types-and-expressions/#Core-C______--Types-and-expressions"}});